  "question": {
    "text": "An alternating voltage of amplitude $40 \\mathrm{~V}$ and frequency $4 \\mathrm{kHz}$ is applied directly across the capacitor of $12 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$. The maximum displacement current between the plates of the capacitor is nearly :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "XOPpY",
      "text": "$10 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GxN8n",
      "text": "$12 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "L9pdi",
      "text": "$8 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "91KhV",
      "text": "$13 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Displacement current is same as conduction current in capacitor.\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& X_C=\\frac{1}{\\omega \\mathrm{C}}=\\frac{1}{2 \\pi \\mathrm{fC}} \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{2 \\pi \\times 4 \\times 10^3 \\times 12 \\times 10^{-6}}=3.317 \\Omega\n\\end{aligned}$\n$I=\\frac{V}{X_C}=\\frac{40}{3.317}=12 \\mathrm{~A}$",
    "image": null
  },
